      "title": "[P2] Propagate failures from the worklist reader",
      "body": "When `bd list` or the worklist's `jq` pipeline fails, its process-substitution status is not propagated to the parent `while`; the loop simply reads no rows and the script reports `Flagged 0 ...` with exit status 0. This makes tracker/database failures indistinguishable from a legitimate empty worklist, so capture and validate the worklist before iterating.",
